# The local seeding harness: a whole library dumped to disk so the app can be driven with no token.
# It is personal data in a public repository, and the hazard git can answer for is the accidental
# commit — a `git add -A` with nothing here sweeps it into history, where a later force-push takes
# it off the branch tips and leaves it fetchable by SHA. `.git/info/exclude` is the wrong place for
# the same rule: it is per-machine, so it protects neither a clone nor a checkout whose exclude file
# has been rewritten by something else.
#
# Matched by prefix rather than by the two names, since the build copies public/ verbatim with no
# per-file opt-out: a seed-2.json dropped here while debugging is published by `npm run deploy`
# exactly as the first one would have been. Better still is to keep the harness out of public/
# altogether, under a directory the build never reads.
public/seed*
